\begin{cor} \label{C: number of red spaces}
Let $\mathcal{F$ be a maximal coclique of $\Gamma_{2n}$ with $n\geq 3$.
Either the number of red $(n-1)$-spaces in $\PG(2n,q)$ is $\mathcal{O(q^{n^2-2})$, or there is a point $P$ and every $(n-1)$-space incident with $P$ is red.\\
Either the number of red $n$-spaces in $\PG(2n,q)$ is $\mathcal{O(q^{n^2-2})$, or there is a hyperplane $H$ and every $n$-space incident with $H$ is red.
\end{cor}

